<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Khandesh Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1382 CE – 1601 CE · capital Burhanpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small sultanate of the Tapti valley ruled by the Faruqi dynasty from Burhanpur and the great fortress of Asirgarh.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-raja-faruqi">Malik Raja Faruqi</a>, a noble granted lands in the Tapti valley by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firuz-shah-tughluq">Firuz Shah Tughluq</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, became effectively independent around 1382 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi's</a> authority collapsed. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-khan-faruqi">Nasir Khan</a> took the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asirgarh-fort">Asirgarh</a> and founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a>, which became the capital of the Faruqi kingdom.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khandesh">Khandesh</a> was a buffer state between the larger <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gujarat-sultanate">Gujarat Sultanate</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/malwa-sultanate">Malwa Sultanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a>, and its rulers survived by shifting alliances and marriages. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a> grew into a busy centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> textiles and trade on the route between north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. The Faruqis built mosques, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jama-masjid-burhanpur">Jama Masjid of Burhanpur</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> demanded submission, and when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahadur-shah-faruqi">Bahadur Shah Faruqi</a> resisted, Mughal armies besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asirgarh-fort">Asirgarh</a>, which surrendered in 1601. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khandesh">Khandesh</a> became a Mughal province, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burhanpur">Burhanpur</a> served as a base for Mughal campaigns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1382 CE – 1601 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:87.20%;width:4.36%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1382 CE – 1601 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Burhanpur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Malik Raja Faruqi, Nasir Khan, Bahadur Shah Faruqi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Farooqi dynasty, Faruqi Sultanate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=khandesh-sultanate" aria-label="Khandesh Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6728 1390 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khandesh Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7048 1646L7018 1385M7048 1646L6939 1584M7048 1646L7018 1385"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7018 1385h0M693